      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: honor configured default agent across main paths",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes the remaining hardcoded `DEFAULT_AGENT_ID = \"main\"` assumptions called out in #90573 for deployments whose configured default agent is not `main`.\n\nPR #30654 fixed the main session-key write paths, but #90573 identified follow-on paths that still synthesized `agents/main/*`, `agent:main:*`, or phantom `main` audit scopes even when config declares a different default agent such as `nova`.\n\nThis PR uses the existing `agents.list[].default` / first-agent behavior. It intentionally does **not** add a new `agents.defaultAgentId` config key or `OPENCLAW_DEFAULT_AGENT_ID` environment variable.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe current behavior makes non-`main` default-agent deployments inconsistent: some surfaces honor the configured default agent, while others silently route storage, session keys, setup directories, or audit reporting through `main`. That creates broken paths and confusing phantom state for multi-agent installs.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDeployments whose configured default agent is not `main` can keep using their chosen default agent without residual `main` paths leaking into session initialization, auth/model storage scans, setup transcript directories, or exec-scope audit output.\n\n## Changes\n\n- Key new explicit `sessionId` sessions to the resolved store/default agent instead of literal `main`.\n- Thread the resolved agent id into auto-reply session initialization.\n- Resolve default auth/model storage scan paths from the configured default agent directory.\n- Stop security audit exec-scope reporting from injecting a phantom `main` default when another agent is configured as default.\n- Avoid inferring a delivery channel from one-segment agent main-session keys when the agent id happens to match a channel name.\n- Let setup create the configured default agent's transcript directory instead of `agents/main/sessions` when config is available.\n\n## Risk Mitigations\n\n- **Compatibility:** no schema/env surface added; legacy `main` aliases are still recognized where they already were.\n- **Auth-provider:** storage discovery still includes existing directories under state plus configured agent dirs; this only replaces the synthetic default path.\n- **Session-state:** new explicit sessions use the same effective default agent that owns the selected store; existing persisted keys are not migrated here.\n\n## Evidence\n\nCurrent head: `8bbd81367e8807a741314b9a91cfb99d24b4586e`.\nCurrent base: `6db0506474ceb10c64ea3b5f64e29772fb04280e`.\n\n### Current-head runtime proof\n\nIsolated config with `main` present and `ops` marked as `agents.list[].default` validates cleanly, and `agents list --json` reports `ops` as the default without promoting `main`:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"main\",\n    \"isDefault\": false,\n    \"agentDir\": \"<home>/.openclaw/agents/main/agent\",\n    \"workspace\": \"<home>/.openclaw/workspace-main\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"id\": \"ops\",\n    \"isDefault\": true,\n    \"agentDir\": \"<home>/.openclaw/agents/ops/agent\",\n    \"workspace\": \"<home>/.openclaw/workspace\"\n  }\n]\n```\n\nDirect runtime proof with configured agents `utility` and default `ops`, plus an existing on-disk `agents/main/agent` store, shows the new default surfaces consistently use `ops` while still discovering the old `main` store:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"defaultAgentId\": \"ops\",\n  \"defaultAgentDir\": \"<state>/agents/ops/agent\",\n  \"sessionKey\": \"agent:ops:main\",\n  \"sessionStorePath\": \"<state>/agents/ops/sessions/sessions.json\",\n  \"transcriptDir\": \"<state>/agents/ops/sessions\",\n  \"authStoreAgentDirs\": [\n    \"<state>/agents/ops/agent\",\n    \"<state>/agents/main/agent\",\n    \"<state>/agents/utility/agent\"\n  ],\n  \"modelsJsonPaths\": [\n    \"<state>/agents/ops/agent/models.json\",\n    \"<state>/agents/main/agent/models.json\",\n    \"<state>/agents/utility/agent/models.json\"\n  ],\n  \"auditFinding\": {\n    \"checkId\": \"agents.claude_cli.permission_mode_overridden_by_yolo\",\n    \"severity\": \"warn\",\n    \"detail\": \"claude-cli sets args=default, but OpenClaw exec is YOLO for: ops, utility, ops. Managed Claude live sessions use --permission-mode bypassPermissions.\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThat covers the requested proof surfaces: session key/store path, setup transcript path, auth/model scan discovery, audit output, and explicit preservation/discovery of an existing `agents/main` store without treating `main` as the configured default.\n\n### Local validation\n\n- Focused default-agent tests: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/secrets/storage-scan.default-agent.test.ts src/agents/command/session.resolve-session-key.test.ts src/auto-reply/reply/session-delivery.test.ts src/config/sessions/paths.default-agent.test.ts src/security/audit-exec-surface.test.ts` — passed 4 Vitest shards / 41 tests on current head.\n- Core typecheck: `node scripts/run-tsgo.mjs -p tsconfig.core.json --incremental --tsBuildInfoFile .artifacts/tsgo-cache/core.tsbuildinfo` — passed on current head.\n- Formatting: `pnpm exec oxfmt --check` over the 14 touched files — passed on current head.\n- Touched-file lint: `pnpm exec oxlint` over the 14 touched files — passed on current head.\n- Whitespace: `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD` — passed on current head.\n- Pre-PR preview: `~/.openclaw/workspace/scripts/openclaw-pre-pr.sh --repo /root/projects/openclaw-pr-51762 --plan-only` completed after rebasing onto current `upstream/main`.\n\nGitHub checks are expected to re-run for this pushed head.\n\nCloses #90573.\nSupersedes stale #17477 without adding the previously proposed config/env fallback surface.",
